{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/785313-fetish-idea-and-creation-help","id":785313,"title":"Fetish idea and creation help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-13T04:20:33-08:00","id":785313,"title":"Fetish idea and creation help","content":"One of my players, who is planning to play Fianna Galliard has decided to start game with guitar which is also a fetish (heirloom passed down from his father who was/is werewolf). And I have hard time deciding what effect will this fetish have.<br /> The first idea was something similar to Head Games, before I noticed that Head Games was Rank 5 Galliard gift and I decided against it, because I think it takes fun out of character progression if you just give players effects similar to Rank 5 gifts at the start of the game:<br /> The second idea is something similar to Command the Gathering/Song of the Siren:<br /> <br /> When player activates fetish and plays it, he rolls Charisma+Performance (difficulty equal to the target's Willpower). All in the earshot whose Willpower is exceeded are affected. Affected targets are compelled to either listen or dance while listening to the song (targets choice). Affected targets are also entranced by the song to such degree that they suffer +2 difficulty to Perception rolls. The effect lasts as long as character plays the fetish. The target can spend Willpower point to break the effect for a scene (and become immune to further uses of the fetish in that scene). Obvious danger also breaks the effect (room on fire, attacks.., etc.).<br /> <br /> I am interested in opinions about this fetish. What would you change about it, if anything? Also I am at the lost on what Level and Gnosis should this fetish have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2310-ophidian","name":"Ophidian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-13T16:56:26-08:00","id":785636,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't worry too much about access to higher Rank Gifts effects. Plenty of Totems allow whole packs to get access to Rank 3-4 Gifts at start. Just keep the Fetish rating higher (which is basically how Hammer &amp; Klaive, the Revised book on making Fetishes, guides you in that regard).<br /> <br /> For the specific effect, it's usually easier to have the difficulty key off the highest Willpower in range, rather than a specific target.<br /> <br /> It's probably in the 2-3 range for Level, and Gnosis 6-8. Though the Gnosis rating is pretty minor since dropping 1 point of Gnosis instead of rolling is going to happen a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T06:22:42-08:00","id":785933,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you want the effect from the old Bone Gnawer Rank 2 gift; Hootenanny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T09:34:35-08:00","id":786037,"title":"","content":"I think denying a rank 5 gift is fine. High ranking gifts in my game are 'gated' by rank as well as quests and chiminage so that the pack's accomplishments mean something.<br /> <br /> That said, Head Games is a pretty tame rank 5 gift- it hardly seems overpowered to allow the Galliard the ability to toy with a single other individual's emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-18T02:49:54-08:00","id":788630,"title":"","content":"You're being reasonable. Level 5 gifts should be gated on principle, even if is a relatively low powered gift like Head Games. Any item that would give the Garou access to such a thing would be something of legend and should come with loads of strings and problems involved.<br /> <br /> The concept for the item is good, I'd put it either at rank 2 or 3, depending on how drastically you interpret the fascination effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}